# Battle Core Mechanics

## Node Control System [done]
- Strategic network nodes must be captured and held
- Control determined by damage dealt to nodes
- Capture threshold set at 75% of total army health
- Tracks accumulated damage per side
- Updates control status after each hit

## Loss Tracking System [done]
- Tracks battalion losses
- Monitors node control changes
- Calculates victory points based on control duration

## Scoring System [done]
- Points awarded for:
  - Node control duration ✓
  - Enemy battalion elimination ✓
  - Network control bonuses ✓

## Victory Determination [done]
- Victory achieved through:
  - Total network control ✓
  - Point threshold reached ✓
  - Enemy force elimination ✓

## State Management System [in-progress]
### Core Principles:
- Single source of truth
- Centralized state management
- Clear ownership of state updates
- Predictable state transitions
- Atomic state operations

### Update Frequency:
- Global 1-second update timer
- Batch related state changes
- Optimize update scheduling
- Handle state dependencies

## Update Timing System [to-do]
### Three-tier hierarchy:
1. Real-time (60fps):
   - Animations, movement, visual effects
   - Uses requestAnimationFrame
   - RAF fallback for background tabs

2. Speed-based:
   - Attack animations (per battalion speed stat)
   - Duration = 1000ms / speed stat
   - Uses Animated.timing with easing

3. Global timer (1s):
   - Health, damage, state synchronization
   - Aligns with backend update cycle
   - Buffers state changes

